From e296da63d3ca53ebef87be8ac6395dac1de40b20 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 22:23:13 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Audit fixes: fail-closed voice webhooks, atomic sign-in
 links, desktop URL policy

- Twilio voice webhooks (incoming, status, after-stream, handoff) now refuse
  requests when the shop has no Twilio token instead of skipping the signature
  check. An unsigned "incoming call" could otherwise obtain a signed AI stream
  on the shop's xAI key and metered minutes. DEV_AUTH_BYPASS=1 still skips it
  for local development; TWILIO_VERIFY_VOICE=0 remains an explicit opt-out.
- Magic-link sign-in claims the link with a conditional UPDATE before creating
  a session, so two simultaneous redemptions can no longer both sign in.
- Desktop: pop-ups only hand https ShopCrank pages to shell.openExternal (never
  file: URLs), and file: navigation is limited to the app's own folder.
  Rules live in desktop/url-policy.js with tests.
- Assistant search-source links accept only http(s) URLs.
- CI now runs tests that no script ran before: record-deletion,
  customer-metrics, perf, shop-entity-load, merge-open-prs, url-policy,
  gemini-assistant.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GGEY5cQcwh34RQLfpVUQwK
