From 2c57d1bf5b5e86e7630bd064dac47325f0d0278f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 02:03:40 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Audit follow-ups: encrypted offline shop file, write-once
 uploads, link cap, cleanup

- Offline desktop: the shop file is encrypted with Windows DPAPI (Electron
  safeStorage) on installed copies; the portable USB edition stays plain so the
  drive opens on any PC. Existing plain files are read and encrypted on the next
  save. A file that cannot be unlocked is set aside, never overwritten.
- Uploads are write-once (R2 onlyIf etagDoesNotMatch '*'): every upload gets a
  fresh key, so no role can replace an existing photo or PDF.
- Signed/approved customer document links stay viewable for a year after
  signing, then expire (they never expired before).
- Removed the broken blackflag-ecu and PowerShell gitlinks (no .gitmodules) and
  ignore both folders; they are separate repositories.
- Removed src/modules/gemini-assistant.js, which nothing imported.

